\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Boundary cells and the declared action}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The [cellular sign model](fdip-00XN) uses the full cochain
operator #{5\bbI+\extD_U}, periodic fields and counting link
weights. Its edge pullback contains source transport, and its
strict half contains only a vertex. A Wilson spinor action
with time projectors, or a reflection that mixes cochain
degrees, would define a different quadratic-form problem.
Positivity for either construction requires its own action,
reflection and observable correspondence.}
